Procurement has to secure the information and assistance that lawful operation needs.

**Possible review fields:**
- intended purpose, system and model version, performance limits and instructions for use under Article 13;
- evidence of the provider role, CE marking and EU declaration of conformity where applicable;
- quality, bias, robustness and security testing proportionate to the risk;
- notification and documentation of material updates;
- access to logs and information the deployer needs for Article 26 and data protection;
- support on risks, incidents, data-subject rights, authority requests, exit and deletion of data.

Reporting frequency, response periods, audit rights, liability, contractual penalties, language, governing law and jurisdiction are negotiation points. In an incident XY GmbH follows Article 26(5); the provider performs its reporting duty under Article 73.
